4. Sabse important architectural decision
Main tumhare existing four-layer architecture ko change karne ki recommendation nahi dunga.
Existing four-layer Foundation ko preserve karo.
Layer 01 — Knowledge and Memory

Company, customer, project, requirements, history

Layer 02 — Context Intelligence

Retrieval, repository, L0–L4, specialist context

Layer 03 — Execution and Agent Infrastructure

8 specialists, models, tools, workflows, recovery

Layer 04 — Quality and Governance

QA, security, permissions, approvals, audit


In sabke upar Company Platform

Internal products + external customer workspaces, dashboard, delivery and billing

Customer isolation, provider security aur execution permissions ko alag-alag afterthought nahi banana chahiye. Unke contracts Foundation ke initial stages se hi design hone chahiye.
5. Final verdict
Tumhara plan weak nahi hai. Ismein company ki core architecture, specialist independence, memory, context, governance aur implementation sequence ki achhi foundation hai.

Lekin abhi ye Architecture and Engineering Plan hai, complete executable engineering specification nahi.

Meri taraf se sabse badi paanch corrections hongi:
1. Multi-tenant customer architecture.
2. Actual specialist execution and handoff contracts.
3. Secure tool execution architecture.
4. Complete context, model and memory integration.
5. Measurable quality, reliability and commercial acceptance criteria.
Mera suggestion: Existing Foundation plan ko bina soche replace nahi karna chahiye. Pehle in gaps ko existing 20 sections ke andar properly integrate karke ek consolidated, versioned architecture baseline banani chahiye. Uske baad implementation karenge, taaki baar-baar architecture aur files replace na karni padein.

Tumhare goal mein sirf apne products banana nahi, balki isi workforce se external customers ke software projects deliver karna bhi shamil hai. Ye dono capabilities ek hi Company OS ka hissa honi chahiye
